{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 41, :comments ["<b>The tied ones.</b> Rashi explained according to the Targum: the firstborn. And it has no support in Scripture. It appears that it is from the language of קשר (tying), for it was a custom in those days that they would tie a knot on the firstborns because of their cherished status, in order to recognize them and so as not to exchange them — just as they would do for a human firstborn, as it is said: ״ותקשור על ידו שני לאמר זה יצא ראשונה״ — for even in our generation it is the way of people to cherish the firstborns and to keep them alive and to leave them more than the others. From Maharam."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:06:21.465332402Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}